## Appendix E Elo Calculation

This appendix gives more detail on the Elo calculation method, which follows a similar setup to [Khan et al. (2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2407.04622v2#bib.bib25). We generate a series of 1-turn arguments in simultaneous debate (i.e. just opening arguments), with five debaters: Gemma7B, GPT-3.5, Gemini Pro 1.0, Gemini Pro 1.5 (all with BoN=1), and Gemini Pro 1.5 with BoN=4. We then sample 512 (with each dataset contributing an equal number) pairings of cross-play debates and judge them with Pro 1.5 to generate a win-rate matrix, ωi,j\omega\_{i,j} where i,ji,j range over the five debaters, representing frequency that debater ii beats debater jj. We then calculate aggregate Elo ranking scores, EiE\_{i} for each debater. To do this, we define the expected win-rate, ω^i\hat{\omega}\_{i}, for debater PiP\_{i}, with Elo EiE\_{i} against PjP\_{j}, with Elo EjE\_{j} as

